<h1>Redirects</h1>
<p>These 301 redirects must be configured manually in <strong>Webflow → Site Settings → Publishing → 301 Redirects</strong>. The Webflow API/MCP cannot create redirects. A Webflow redirect only fires for a path that no longer resolves to a live page, so each source page below has already been unpublished.</p>
<h2>Active redirects</h2>
<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>Source (old path)</th><th>Target (new path)</th><th>Reason</th><th>Date added</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>/services/whooping-cough</code></td>
<td><code>/services/flu-vaccination</code></td>
<td>The "Whooping Cough Immunization &amp; PCR Tests" service was retired. Whooping cough immunisation is now a subsection of the Flu Vaccination page; PCR testing has been discontinued.</td>
<td>2026-07-13</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Locale variants</h2>
<p>Secondary locales publish under subdirectories (<code>/zh</code>, <code>/ko</code>). If the retired page was indexed in those locales, add matching redirects:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>/zh/services/whooping-cough</code> &rarr; <code>/zh/services/flu-vaccination</code></li>
<li><code>/ko/services/whooping-cough</code> &rarr; <code>/ko/services/flu-vaccination</code></li>
</ul>
<p><em>Confirm the exact live path in Webflow before saving &mdash; service pages resolve under the Services collection's URL prefix (<code>/services/&lt;slug&gt;</code>).</em></p>
